-- Verified knowledge for three product topics (ChatGPT decision 2026-11-18, relayed by HQ Agents): CSV import, and the exact free-trial rule.
-- (The Edge Score's five parts and renormalisation are already in 0055.) Source: the reviewed Verified facts register in the fillbook repo,
-- scripts/command-center/knowledge/product-facts.md (merged 21749f1, reviewed 2026-11-18), which cites the code. Site Work is the source of truth.
-- Additive and idempotent: each row is added only if no verified entry for its topic exists. Nothing is deleted or deprecated.
-- Growth OS migrations have no runner: the owner applies this by hand in the Supabase SQL editor (project fillbook-growth-os).

insert into knowledge_documents (topic, title, content, source_doc, trust_level, effective_at)
select 'csv_import', 'CSV import: how the importer works (verified 2026-11-18)',
  $$Fillbook imports trades from a CSV export, for the platforms that do not have automatic sync. CSV import needs no broker login and never connects to a broker. How the import wizard works, in order: (1) a searchable, grouped source picker; picking a source is optional, because Fillbook recognises most platforms from the file's columns; (2) "Export your trades from" the chosen source, with step-by-step export guides, and then the trader drops the file in; reading the file happens in the browser, and only the trades the trader confirms are saved to the account; (3) if the file matches a format Fillbook recognises, it says it recognised the format and mapped it automatically. Otherwise it says it could not find some fields automatically and shows a screen where the trader confirms the column mapping by picking the matching column for each field; (4) a review screen shows the destination account ("Import into"), the detected format, how the file's dates and timezone were read (a time zone picker appears when the file has no zone), and gross, fees, commissions and net. Nothing is saved until the trader confirms. For formats with a documented P&L basis Fillbook compares its computed net with the file's reported total and shows any difference; for most formats no comparison is made, so never say Fillbook reconciles every import; (5) the done screen lists the rejected row numbers, counting the header as row 1, with the reasons: an unreadable date, a blank or zero price or quantity, or an empty symbol or date cell. Some exports, for example TopstepX or ProjectX, contain no account identifier, so the trader must choose the destination account. Undo import is a separate feature. There is also an optional, private button to send an unreadable file to Fillbook support, shown only when a format is unreadable, so never say or imply that nothing is sent anywhere. Never call CSV import or any file the trader must re-export "auto-sync". Being listed in the source picker is not evidence a format was tested, so never say a broker or firm is "supported" or "tested". Never give a broker-specific export click path.$$,
  'fillbook:scripts/command-center/knowledge/product-facts.md (reviewed 2026-11-18) citing frontend/src/lib/csvImport.ts and ImportWizard.tsx; step order confirmed by Site Work 2026-11-18', 'verified', now()
where not exists (select 1 from knowledge_documents where topic = 'csv_import' and trust_level = 'verified');

insert into knowledge_documents (topic, title, content, source_doc, trust_level, effective_at)
select 'free_trial_rule', 'Free trial rule (verified 2026-11-18)',
  $$Every new account gets a 14-day free trial, and no card is needed. If the trader has not brought in a trade yet, the trial stays open until the first trades arrive, for up to about 90 days after sign-up, and the 14 days start then. If the first trade arrives after sign-up, the 14 days start over from that day. This happens once per account, whichever way the trade arrives (import, sync or add-on). The trial includes automatic sync for one broker or platform connection, drawdown alerts and the analytics. It does not include AI coaching, the Discord daily recap, Trade Replay, mentor links, accountability share links or the AI-assistant connection; those need a paid plan. When the 14 days end the dashboard says so and shows what the trial found in the trader's own trades; the trader is never charged without choosing a plan, and the account steps down to the permanent Free plan, which keeps manual and CSV logging and the drawdown, daily-loss and consistency buffer for one account (auto-sync and drawdown alerts need Core or Elite). Say "drawdown alerts" for the alerts that warn as an account approaches its rule limits; a limit is "hit" or "touched", never "breached". Never say real-time. Never state a trade limit or a price for the Free plan; point to the Billing or pricing page.$$,
  'fillbook:scripts/command-center/knowledge/product-facts.md (reviewed 2026-11-18) citing the trial migrations 20261112a and 20261113a, trialConnections.ts and plan.ts', 'verified', now()
where not exists (select 1 from knowledge_documents where topic = 'free_trial_rule' and trust_level = 'verified');
